  "description": "MEVNAF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C99 H107 Er6 N10 O32 1+,C2 H3 O2 1-,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er6 (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.477-3.770 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.30-113.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C101H112N10O35Er6.",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
